    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p47-q32-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Using the fact that $\\sin x<x<\\tan x$ for $0<x<\\frac{\\pi}{2}$, explain why $x^2\\sin x<x^3<x^2\\tan x$ for $0<x<\\frac{\\pi}{2}$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Since $x^2>0$, multiplying the given inequality by $x^2$ preserves its direction: $x^2\\sin x<x^3<x^2\\tan x$.",
          "worked": "For $0<x<\\frac{\\pi}{2}$, $\\sin x<x<\\tan x$ and $x^2>0$. Multiplying through by $x^2$ gives\n$$x^2\\sin x<x^3<x^2\\tan x.$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      },
      {
        "id": "p47-q32-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence show that $\\displaystyle\\int_0^{\\pi/4}x^2\\sin x\\,dx<\\frac{\\pi^4}{4^5}<\\int_0^{\\pi/4}x^2\\tan x\\,dx$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\displaystyle\\int_0^{\\pi/4}x^2\\sin x\\,dx<\\int_0^{\\pi/4}x^3\\,dx=\\frac{\\pi^4}{4^5}<\\int_0^{\\pi/4}x^2\\tan x\\,dx$.",
          "worked": "Integrating the inequality from part a over $0\\le x\\le\\frac{\\pi}{4}$ preserves strict inequalities because they are strict throughout the interior:\n$$\\begin{aligned}\n\\int_0^{\\pi/4}x^2\\sin x\\,dx&<\\left[\\frac{x^4}{4}\\right]_0^{\\pi/4}<\\int_0^{\\pi/4}x^2\\tan x\\,dx\\\\\n\\int_0^{\\pi/4}x^2\\sin x\\,dx&<\\frac{\\pi^4}{4^5}<\\int_0^{\\pi/4}x^2\\tan x\\,dx.\n\\end{aligned}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 25
      }
    ]
  },
